(SECTION 2: BEARING INSPECTION & LUBRICATION PROCEDURES) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -25 Td
(2.1 Bearing Degradation Symptoms) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Common symptoms of rolling element bearing wear include high-frequency acoustic squealing,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(inner race spalling harmonics at BPFI \(Ball Pass Frequency Inner race\), outer race defects at BPFO,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(and localized bearing housing temperature exceeding 75 degrees Celsius.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(2.2 Recommended Inspection Steps for Bearing Problems) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Step 1: Perform acoustic ultrasound listening check for periodic impacts or clicking.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Step 2: Measure overall RMS vibration velocity and acceleration enveloping peak-to-peak.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Step 3: Measure thermal infrared gradient across drive-end \(DE\) and non-drive-end \(NDE\) bearings.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Step 4: Inspect grease sample for metallic particle discoloration or oxidation degradation.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Step 5: Check shaft axial and radial play with dial indicator \(< 0.05 mm allowable\).) Tj
0 -14 Td
ET
endstream
endobj
